{"challenges":[{"attack":"Verify that the cited substring exactly matches the supplied dispatch source and that the claim does not assert the shipment occurred as a fact.","claim_id":"dispatch-record","outcome":"survives","result":"shipment-count[0:41] is exactly \"Dispatch record: 12 cartons were shipped.\" The claim is correctly limited to what the record states.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Verify the cited packing substring and whether it explicitly names the dispatch record.","claim_id":"packing-record","outcome":"survives","result":"units-per-carton[0:70] is exactly \"Packing specification for this shipment: each carton contains 8 units.\" It attributes that statement to the packing record, but does not itself link it to shipment-count.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Verify the cited damage substring and whether it identifies the dispatched shipment.","claim_id":"damage-record","outcome":"survives","result":"damage-record[0:69] is exactly \"Receiving record: 3 units were damaged in transit and are not usable.\" It contains no shipment identifier.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Check whether any supplied text explicitly cross-references the dispatch and receiving records.","claim_id":"linkage-limitation","outcome":"survives","result":"The complete cited dispatch and receiving strings contain no shared identifier or explicit cross-reference. The limitation follows from the supplied text comparison.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Attempt to infer the same-shipment condition from the records alone.","claim_id":"same-shipment-assumption","outcome":"survives","result":"The condition is explicitly labeled an assumption and is not presented as an established fact. It remains necessary and unproved.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Check whether the cited carton specification is explicitly linked to the 12-carton dispatch before multiplying.","claim_id":"original-units","outcome":"fails","result":"The arithmetic 12 × 8 = 96 is correct, but shipment-count[0:41] and units-per-carton[0:70] do not explicitly identify the same shipment. Thus 96 is not established without an additional dispatch-to-packing linkage assumption.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Check whether the stated same-shipment assumption supplies every premise needed for 96 − 3 = 93.","claim_id":"usable-units","outcome":"fails","result":"The assumption links the damage count to the dispatched shipment, but it does not link the packing specification to that dispatch. Since original-units is unsupported as written, 93 needs an additional assumption that the 8-units-per-carton specification applies to the 12 dispatched cartons.","tool_ids":[]}],"checks":[{"basis_reasoning":"The source substring mechanically supports an attribution of this wording to the supplied dispatch record; it does not establish the real-world event independently.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"dispatch-record","reasoning":"The citation matches shipment-count[0:41] exactly. The statement is limited to record content.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The source substring mechanically supports an attribution of this wording to the supplied packing record; it does not establish that the referenced shipment is the dispatch in another source.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"packing-record","reasoning":"The citation matches units-per-carton[0:70] exactly. The statement is limited to record content.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The source substring mechanically supports an attribution of this wording to the supplied receiving record; it does not establish that the record concerns the dispatch.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"damage-record","reasoning":"The citation matches damage-record[0:69] exactly. The statement is limited to record content.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The cited full dispatch and receiving texts were compared in linkage-limit-step. Neither supplies an explicit cross-record identifier or reference.","basis_verdict":"applicable","checked_step_ids":["linkage-limit-step"],"claim_id":"linkage-limitation","reasoning":"This is a self-contained textual deduction about the supplied records, not a claim that the records concern different shipments.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"This is expressly an added assumption, not source-established evidence, and no proof step discharges it.","basis_verdict":"conditional","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"same-shipment-assumption","reasoning":"The draft appropriately preserves uncertainty by marking the condition as an assumption.","verdict":"conditional"},{"basis_reasoning":"original-units-step correctly performs 12 × 8, but its cited records lack an explicit premise connecting the 8-unit specification to the 12-carton dispatch.","basis_verdict":"unsupported","checked_step_ids":["original-units-step"],"claim_id":"original-units","reasoning":"Arithmetic alone cannot establish that these two values describe the same shipment. The claim requires an additional linkage assumption.","verdict":"unsupported"},{"basis_reasoning":"usable-units-step correctly computes 96 − 3 under inclusion of the damaged units, but its dependency original-units is unsupported and the stated assumption does not repair the packing-to-dispatch gap.","basis_verdict":"unsupported","checked_step_ids":["original-units-step","usable-units-step"],"claim_id":"usable-units","reasoning":"The conclusion would be conditional on both record linkages: packing-to-dispatch and damage-to-dispatch.","verdict":"unsupported"}],"missing_evidence":["An explicit identifier or other linkage showing that units-per-carton[0:70] applies to the 12 cartons in shipment-count[0:41].","An explicit identifier or other linkage showing that damage-record[0:69] concerns that same dispatched shipment and that its three units are included in the shipment total."],"recommended_action":"revise","tool_requests":[]}
